<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador's Jan oil output up 1.3 pct vs yr ago.</title>
<headline>Ecuador's Jan oil output up 1.3 pct vs yr ago.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador produced an average of 385,152 barrels per day (bpd) of crude oil in January, up 1.3 percent from the same month last year, an official said Tuesday.</p>
<p>An official from the National Hydrocarbon Office, who asked not to be named, said that in January 1996 the country produced an average of 380,075 bpd.</p>
<p>Oil production in Ecuador was an average of 383,858 bpd last year.</p>
<p>((--Gustavo Oviedo, Quito Newsroom, 5932 258429))</p>
